  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="ES">Agricultura</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Biofortified Maize Program</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Guatemala):  ..The Farming for Nutrition activity, a public-private partnership, expands biofortified maize production in Guatemala to establish a sustainable market for high-yield, high-nutrient maize seeds. Biofortified maize, enriched with higher nutritional value than regular maize, aims to boost smallholder farmer incomes, enhance climate resilience, and improve nutrition among rural families, particularly vulnerable groups. By addressing poverty and malnutrition, the activity aligns with U.S. goals to promote regional stability, economic security, and reduced irregular migration...With FY 2024 funds, the activity will partner with the Government of Guatemala and the private sector to develop and launch biofortified maize seeds with commercial potential building local breeding capacity and fostering self-reliance; increase rural incomes and improve nutrition by addressing chronic deficits through expanded access to biofortified maize; and institutionalize seed access via a government-supported subsidy ensuring sustainable food security for smallholder farmers...USAID will collaborate with the Inter-American Institute for Cooperation on Agriculture (IICA), the Institute of Nutrition of Central America and Panama (INCAP), and the University of Wisconsin. These partners bring expertise in nutrition science, sustainable agriculture, and community development, supporting technical assistance, development, and testing of biofortified maize hybrids. The activity will improve income and nutrition for 14,000 farming families, scaling up to 43,000 families by its conclusion and benefiting an estimated 1.3 million rural consumers. ..The activity aligns with the Integrated Country Strategy Mission Goals 1 and 3, CDCS 2020-2025 Development Objectives 1 and 2, and Pillar 1 of the U.S. Strategy for Addressing the Root Causes of Migration. .. .</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="ES">La agricultura es la ciencia y la pr&#xe1;ctica de la producci&#xf3;n de alimentos, piensos y fibras (incluida la silvicultura, la vida silvestre, la pesca, la acuicultura y la flora) y sus relaciones con los recursos naturales, el procesamiento, la comercializaci&#xf3;n, la distribuci&#xf3;n, la utilizaci&#xf3;n (incluida la nutrici&#xf3;n) y el comercio.</narrative>
  </description>
